---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { webAppUrl } from "../lib/web-app-url.mjs";

const webApp = webAppUrl(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_WEB_APP_URL);
---

<Base title="Delete your account (draft) - Plate & Bar" description="How to delete your Plate & Bar account and data. Draft, pending lawyer review.">
  <div class="doc"><div class="prose">
  <h1>Delete your account</h1>
  <div class="draft" role="note" aria-label="Draft notice">
    <p><strong>DRAFT. Pending lawyer review under India's Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023.</strong></p>
    <p>This is a placeholder and is not legally reviewed. It must not be relied on until this notice is removed.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Delete in the app</h2>
  {!webApp && <p>This is the way to delete your account.</p>}
  <p>Withdrawing your consent means deleting your account, and you can delete your account at any time from "Your data" in the app.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Open the app, go to "Your data" and choose "Delete everything".</li>
    <li>If this device is linked to an account and you are signed out, sign in first. Deleting only the device would leave your account and its server data in place.</li>
    <li>Confirm. The app deletes your account and everything the server stores for it, signs you out and clears the data on this device. It needs a connection.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Before you delete, "Your data" can also download a copy of your data.</p>

  {webApp && (
    <>
      <h2>Delete on the web</h2>
      <p>If you do not have the app on your phone, or you uninstalled it, you can delete your account in the web app. It works the same way.</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Open the <a href={webApp}>web app</a>.</li>
        <li>Tap "Sign in to sync" at the top of the screen, enter the email address of your account, then the 6-digit code we email you.</li>
        <li>On Targets, choose "Download or delete my data". On "Your data", choose "Delete everything".</li>
        <li>Confirm. The web app deletes your account and everything the server stores for it, signs you out and clears the data in this browser. It needs a connection.</li>
      </ol>
    </>
  )}

  <h2>What gets deleted</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>On our server, immediately and with no undo: your account, your email sign-in identity, all sessions, all synced records, the conflict log copies, your daily AI usage counters and, for your email address, any pending one-time codes and records of wrong codes kept for rate limiting.</li>
    <li>Not deleted: one anonymous monthly total of AI tokens (the month and the token count only, with no user id) kept to enforce the shared AI budget. It cannot be linked to your account, so your AI use still counts toward that month's budget. Server logs are also not deleted; see below.</li>
    <li>Also kept: your account's random id and the time of deletion, with nothing else, in an erasure ledger for 45 days, so that restoring a backup cannot bring your account back.</li>
    <li>On the device you delete from: your profile and targets, consent record, food, water and workout logs (including sets and lift history), day notes, weights, measurements, your own foods, recipes and kitchen tests, exclusions, swaps, settings and anything waiting to sync.</li>
    <li>Other devices where you were signed in are signed out the next time they contact the server. Data already on them stays on them until you clear it there.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What is kept, and for how long</h2>
  <p>[Planned policy to confirm: nightly backups are not edited, and your data disappears from them when they expire, at most 30 days after deletion.] Server logs record opaque user ids with operational events (never food, weight, health answers or tokens) and expire after a bounded retention period: the API's own logs and the web server's error lines are kept for at most 14 days, and for less if the logs reach about 200 MB on the server. Web server access logs hold no user id and are kept for at most about 15 days. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>If you cannot use the app</h2>
  <p>This is a manual request handled by a person, not an automatic process, and we do not delete anything on the strength of the sender address alone. In-app deletion is faster and immediate, so use it if you can.</p>
  <ol>
    <li>Email [privacy contact email] with the subject "Delete my account" from the email address of the account.</li>
    <li>We send a one-time code to that address.</li>
    <li>Reply with the code. Only then do we delete the account, and we confirm when it is done. Draft target: within 30 days of the confirmed request.</li>
  </ol>
  </div></div>
</Base>
